---

<DocShell
   title="CLI reference"
   summary="<p>Every <code>a1</code> command and option. <code>a1 &lt;command&gt; --help</code> prints the same information in the terminal, and <code>a1 help-all</code> prints all of it at once.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="commands">All commands</h2>
      <p>
         The command is <code>a1</code>, also installed as <code>a11ied</code>. To run it
         without installing, use <code>npx a11ied</code> in its place.
      </p>
      <h3>Find and fix problems</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><a href="#check"><code>a1 check</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Scan one page and list what to fix and what to check by hand.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#axe"><code>a1 axe</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Run axe-core against one or more pages.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#tree"><code>a1 tree</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Print a page's accessibility tree.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#capture"><code>a1 capture</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Screenshot a page at a viewport, zoom, focus stop, or opened state.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#audit"><code>a1 audit</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Track a WCAG audit that your AI agents carry out, and write the report.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Drive a screen reader</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><a href="#sr"><code>a1 sr</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Read a page as VoiceOver, NVDA, or the simulated screen reader does.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#talkback"><code>a1 talkback</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Turn TalkBack on or off on an Android device and print what it says.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Look things up</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><a href="#wcag"><code>a1 wcag</code></a></dt>
         <dd>WCAG criteria, techniques, and axe rules.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#pattern"><code>a1 pattern</code></a></dt>
         <dd>ARIA patterns: keyboard support and required attributes.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#wcag"><code>a1 search</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Search criteria and patterns together.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Set up and connect</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><a href="#doctor"><code>a1 doctor</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Check the browser and screen reader setup.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#setup"><code>a1 setup</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Install <code>a1</code>, add it to your AI coding agents, and set up VoiceOver or NVDA.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#update"><code>a1 update</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Install the latest version of a11ied.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#other"><code>a1 mcp</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Start the MCP server for AI agents.</dd>
         <dt><a href="#other"><code>a1 help-all</code></a></dt>
         <dd>Print every command's help.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="shared">Shared options</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--json</code></dt>
         <dd>Print one JSON object in place of text. See <a href="/guides/scripting#json">JSON output</a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--verbose</code></dt>
         <dd>Print more detail in text output.</dd>
         <dt><code>--wcag &lt;version&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>2.2</code>, the default, or <code>2.1</code>. On <code>wcag</code>, <code>axe</code>, <code>check</code>, and <code>audit init</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>-V</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>a1</code> alone, print the version.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Naming a page</h3>
      <p><code>check</code>, <code>axe</code>, <code>tree</code>, and <code>pattern check</code> take a page in four ways.</p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>A URL</dt>
         <dd><code>http://localhost:3000/checkout</code></dd>
         <dt>A file path</dt>
         <dd><code>src/components/dialog.html</code></dd>
         <dt><code>-</code></dt>
         <dd>HTML from standard input.</dd>
         <dt><code>--html &lt;markup&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Inline HTML.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         They share these options for getting the page ready. <code>pattern check</code>
         takes all but <code>--wait-for</code>.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--timeout &lt;ms&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>How long the page may take to load. Default 10000.</dd>
         <dt><code>--wait-for &lt;css&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Wait for an element before testing.</dd>
         <dt><code>--click &lt;selector&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Click one element after the page loads, before testing. Opens a dialog or menu that is not on the page until then.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         After a page loads, a1 waits up to three seconds for animations to finish. An
         animation that repeats forever is not waited for.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="check">a1 check</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 check [target] [options]</code></pre>
      <p>
         Scans one page with axe, summarizes its accessibility tree, and lists the
         <a href="/relevant-criteria">criteria that apply</a>. This is the command to start
         with on a page you are building.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--level &lt;level&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Check WCAG through <code>A</code>, <code>AA</code>, or <code>AAA</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--fail-on &lt;impact&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Exit 4 only for violations at or above <code>minor</code>, <code>moderate</code>, <code>serious</code>, or <code>critical</code>. Default: any violation.</dd>
         <dt><code>--baseline &lt;file&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A file of accepted findings that do not count. See <a href="/guides/scripting#baseline">baselines</a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--update-baseline</code></dt>
         <dd>Write the current violations to the baseline file.</dd>
         <dt><code>--format &lt;format&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>text</code>, <code>json</code>, or <code>earl</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--out &lt;file&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Write the report to a file.</dd>
         <dt><code>--storage-state &lt;file&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A saved Playwright sign-in state, for a page behind a login.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 check http://localhost:3000/checkout
a1 check http://localhost:3000/checkout --click "#open-cart" --fail-on serious
a1 check --html '&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;' --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         Exit 0 means the scan found nothing. It does not mean a criterion passes. The JSON
         <code>result</code> has <code>axe</code>, <code>tree</code>, <code>relevance</code>,
         <code>criteria</code>, <code>verdict</code>, and <code>nextCommands</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="axe">a1 axe</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 axe [targets...] [options]</code></pre>
      <p>
         Runs axe-core against one or more pages. With no rule options, it runs every rule
         that maps to a WCAG criterion.
      </p>
      <h3>Choose rules</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--level &lt;level&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Rules for one WCAG level and the levels below it.</dd>
         <dt><code>--criterion &lt;criterion&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Rules for one criterion, by number or slug.</dd>
         <dt><code>--rule &lt;ruleId...&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Named axe rules. This is how to run a best-practice rule such as <code>heading-order</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Scope the page</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--selector &lt;css&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Scan only inside matching elements.</dd>
         <dt><code>--exclude &lt;css&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Leave matching elements out.</dd>
         <dt><code>--viewport &lt;WxH&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The browser viewport, such as <code>1280x800</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--header &lt;header...&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A request header, as <code>'Name: value'</code>. Repeatable.</dd>
         <dt><code>--cookie &lt;cookie...&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A cookie, as <code>'name=value'</code>. Repeatable.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Verdict and output</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--fail-on</code>, <code>--baseline</code>, <code>--update-baseline</code></dt>
         <dd>As for <a href="#check"><code>a1 check</code></a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--format &lt;format&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>text</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>sarif</code>, or <code>earl</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--out &lt;file&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Write the report to a file.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 axe http://localhost:3000 --level AA
a1 axe http://localhost:3000 --criterion 1.4.3
a1 axe http://localhost:3000 --rule heading-order --rule region
a1 axe http://localhost:3000/a http://localhost:3000/b --json
a1 axe http://localhost:3000 --format sarif --out results.sarif</code></pre>
      <p>
         The result has <code>violations</code>, <code>passes</code>, <code>incomplete</code>
         for checks axe could not decide, and <code>inapplicable</code>. With several
         targets, JSON has one report per target under <code>targets</code>. See
         <a href="/guides/violations">fix scan failures</a>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="tree">a1 tree</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 tree [target] [options]</code></pre>
      <p>
         Prints the accessibility tree: the role and name of everything a screen reader can
         reach, as the browser computed them.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--role &lt;role&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Keep nodes with this role, and their ancestors.</dd>
         <dt><code>--name &lt;text&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Keep nodes whose name contains this text, and their ancestors.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 tree http://localhost:3000 --role button
a1 tree http://localhost:3000 --name "Sign in" --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         Text output is Playwright's aria snapshot. <code>--json</code> gives
         <code>result.nodes</code>, a tree of <code>role</code>, <code>name</code>,
         <code>level</code>, and <code>children</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="capture">a1 capture</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 capture &lt;url&gt; --out &lt;file.png&gt; [options]</code></pre>
      <p>
         Loads a page, puts it in a condition, and saves a screenshot. It also prints which
         element has keyboard focus, whether that element is in view or covered, its outline,
         and how far the page overflows sideways. Steps run in this order: wait, click,
         press, hover, capture.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--viewport &lt;WxH&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Viewport in CSS pixels. Default <code>1280x900</code>. To test reflow, use <code>320x800</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--zoom &lt;factor&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Browser zoom, such as <code>2</code> for 200 percent.</dd>
         <dt><code>--text-spacing</code></dt>
         <dd>Apply the text spacing of WCAG 1.4.12.</dd>
         <dt><code>--click &lt;selector&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Click an element first. Repeatable, in order.</dd>
         <dt><code>--press &lt;key&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Press a key. Repeatable. <code>"Tab*5"</code> presses Tab five times.</dd>
         <dt><code>--hover &lt;selector&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Hover an element before the capture.</dd>
         <dt><code>--selector &lt;selector&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Capture one element, outlined, with some of the page around it.</dd>
         <dt><code>--full-page</code></dt>
         <dd>Capture the whole scrollable page.</dd>
         <dt><code>--wait-for &lt;css&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Wait for an element before the first step.</dd>
         <dt><code>--storage-state &lt;file&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A saved Playwright sign-in state.</dd>
         <dt><code>--timeout &lt;ms&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>A limit for each step. Default 30000.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 capture https://example.com --viewport 320x800 --full-page --out reflow.png
a1 capture https://example.com --press "Tab*4" --out focus-4.png</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="sr">a1 sr</h2>
      <p>
         Drives a screen reader through a session. One session is active at a time. See
         <a href="/guides/screen-reader">test with a screen reader</a> for a walk through
         these commands.
      </p>
      <h3>Start and stop</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>sr start [url]</code></dt>
         <dd>Start a session, replacing any active one. Options below.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr open &lt;url&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Load another page in the session.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr status</code></dt>
         <dd>Print the session's screen reader, URL, uptime, and transcript size.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr stop</code></dt>
         <dd>Stop the session. <code>--out &lt;path&gt;</code> writes the transcript, as <code>.md</code> or <code>.json</code>, or as <code>--format</code> says. <code>--session-id &lt;id&gt;</code> retries a stop that failed.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>Options for <code>sr start</code>:</p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--sr &lt;reader&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>virtual</code>, <code>voiceover</code>, or <code>nvda</code>. Without it: the platform's screen reader when it is set up, otherwise <code>virtual</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--browser &lt;name&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>chrome</code>, <code>edge</code>, <code>brave</code>, <code>chromium</code>, or an app name such as <code>Safari</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--app &lt;name&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Read a native app that is already open, in place of a page.</dd>
         <dt><code>--recording &lt;path&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Record the screen to a <code>.mov</code> or <code>.mp4</code> file.</dd>
         <dt><code>--idle-timeout &lt;minutes&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Stop after this many idle minutes. Default 30. <code>0</code> turns it off.</dd>
         <dt><code>--native-input &lt;policy&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>guarded</code>, the default, checks that the session's window is in front before each command. <code>require-binding</code> sends nothing unless the document under the cursor can be verified. <code>development</code> skips the checks.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Move and read</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>sr next [kind]</code>, <code>sr previous [kind]</code></dt>
         <dd>Move one element, or jump by kind: <code>item</code> for any element, <code>heading</code>, <code>link</code>, <code>landmark</code>, <code>control</code>, <code>button</code>, <code>table</code>, <code>list</code>, <code>graphic</code>, <code>region</code>, <code>form-field</code>. <code>--level &lt;1-6&gt;</code> for headings, <code>--times &lt;n&gt;</code> to repeat.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr top</code>, <code>sr bottom</code></dt>
         <dd>Move to the start or end of the page or the current group.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr read</code></dt>
         <dd>Print the current element without moving.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr title</code></dt>
         <dd>Print the page title.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr find &lt;text&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Move to the next element containing the text. Exits 4 when there is none.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr goto</code></dt>
         <dd>Move forward to an element matching <code>--role</code>, <code>--name</code>, or both. <code>--max</code> caps the steps, 500 by default. Exits 4 when there is none.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr elements &lt;kind&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>List every element of one kind from the top. <code>--max</code>, default 200.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr table &lt;move&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd><code>next-cell</code>, <code>previous-cell</code>, <code>next-row</code>, <code>previous-row</code>, <code>next-column</code>, <code>previous-column</code>, <code>row-header</code>, <code>column-header</code>. VoiceOver has no <code>row-header</code> command, and NVDA speaks headers as the cursor enters a cell, so those moves exit 2 there.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr read-all</code></dt>
         <dd>Read from the cursor to the end of the page. <code>--max</code>, default 500.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr walk [url]</code></dt>
         <dd>Read a whole page from the top and print the transcript. Starts a session if needed. Takes <code>--sr</code>, <code>--max</code>, <code>--out</code>, <code>--format</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Use controls</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>sr activate</code></dt>
         <dd>Press the current element.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr interact</code>, <code>sr stop-interacting</code></dt>
         <dd>Step into a group or control, and back out.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr escape</code></dt>
         <dd>Press Escape.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr press &lt;chord...&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Press keys in order. See <a href="#keys">key names</a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr type &lt;text&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Type text.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr do &lt;command&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Run a named screen reader command. <code>--command-set</code> picks <code>auto</code>, <code>portable</code>, <code>voiceover-commander</code>, or <code>voiceover-keycode</code> on macOS, and <code>nvda-keycode</code> on Windows.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr list</code></dt>
         <dd>List the commands <code>sr do</code> takes. <code>--query</code> filters them by text, <code>--sr</code> by screen reader, and <code>--command-set</code> by set.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr focus</code></dt>
         <dd>Bring the session's window to the front. <code>--app</code> or <code>--bundle-id</code> on macOS, <code>--process</code> or <code>--pid</code> on Windows, or <code>--window-title</code> names another. <code>--match</code> compares the title as <code>contains</code> or <code>exact</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Check and record</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>sr checkpoint &lt;label&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Mark a point in the transcript.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr expect &lt;text|/regex/&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Check that something was announced. <code>--since &lt;checkpoint&gt;</code>, <code>--not</code>. Exits 4 on failure.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr wait</code></dt>
         <dd><code>--for &lt;text|/regex/&gt;</code> waits for an announcement and exits 4 at <code>--timeout</code>, default 5000 ms. <code>--since &lt;checkpoint&gt;</code> also counts what was announced after a checkpoint. <code>--ms</code> pauses.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr transcript</code></dt>
         <dd>Print what was said. <code>--since</code>, <code>--tail</code>, <code>--after-index</code>, <code>--limit</code>, <code>--out</code>, <code>--format</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr tail</code></dt>
         <dd>Print announcements as they happen. <code>--lines</code>, default 10, <code>--since</code>, and <code>--interval</code>, default 250 ms. Also named <code>follow</code>, <code>stream</code>, and <code>watch</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr screenshot &lt;path&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Save a picture of the element under the VoiceOver cursor. VoiceOver only.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr batch [file]</code></dt>
         <dd>Run steps from a file or standard input, one JSON object per line. <code>--continue</code> runs the remaining steps after a failed <code>expect</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         Most <code>sr</code> commands also take <code>--phrase</code>, to print the
         announcement alone, and <code>--timeout &lt;ms&gt;</code>. <code>press</code>,
         <code>type</code>, and <code>do</code> take <code>--ephemeral</code>, to run one
         action in a session that stops afterwards.
      </p>
      <p>
         <code>walk</code>, <code>press</code>, <code>type</code>, and <code>do</code> start
         a session when none is active. <code>list</code> needs none, and
         <code>status</code> reports that there is none and exits 0. Every other command
         needs a session. Without one it exits 2, except <code>expect</code>, which exits 3.
      </p>
      <p>
         With <code>--json</code>, every result has <code>result.state</code>:
         <code>lastSpokenPhrase</code>, <code>currentItem</code> with its role, name, value,
         and states, the <code>transcript</code> so far, and <code>observations</code> about
         keyboard focus and the window.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="keys">Key names</h2>
      <p>
         <code>sr press</code> takes one chord per argument. Join the keys of a chord with
         <code>+</code>.
      </p>
      <pre><code>a1 sr press Tab Tab Enter
a1 sr press Shift+Tab
a1 sr press "VO+ArrowRight"</code></pre>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>Modifiers</dt>
         <dd><code>Shift</code>, <code>Control</code>, <code>Alt</code></dd>
         <dt>Letters and digits</dt>
         <dd><code>a</code> to <code>z</code>, <code>0</code> to <code>9</code></dd>
         <dt>Arrows</dt>
         <dd><code>ArrowUp</code>, <code>ArrowDown</code>, <code>ArrowLeft</code>, <code>ArrowRight</code></dd>
         <dt>Navigation</dt>
         <dd><code>Tab</code>, <code>Enter</code>, <code>Escape</code>, <code>Space</code>, <code>Backspace</code>, <code>Delete</code>, <code>Home</code>, <code>End</code>, <code>PageUp</code>, <code>PageDown</code></dd>
         <dt>VoiceOver</dt>
         <dd><code>VO</code> for Control and Option together, <code>Command</code>, <code>Option</code>, <code>Fn</code></dd>
         <dt>NVDA</dt>
         <dd><code>NVDA</code> for Insert, <code>Windows</code>, <code>NumPad0</code> to <code>NumPad9</code></dd>
      </dl>
      <p><code>a1 sr press --help</code> lists every name your platform accepts.</p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="talkback">a1 talkback</h2>
      <p>
         Drives TalkBack on an Android phone, or on an emulator with a Google Play image,
         through <code>adb</code>. TalkBack has to log what it says: set TalkBack settings,
         Advanced settings, Developer settings, Log output level to VERBOSE, once per device.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>talkback on</code>, <code>talkback off</code></dt>
         <dd>Turn TalkBack on or off.</dd>
         <dt><code>talkback walk</code></dt>
         <dd>Press a key several times and print what TalkBack said after each press. <code>--key</code> is <code>next</code>, <code>previous</code>, <code>activate</code>, <code>up</code>, or <code>down</code>. <code>--count</code> defaults to 10.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>Add <code>--serial &lt;id&gt;</code> when more than one device is attached.</p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="wcag">a1 wcag and a1 search</h2>
      <p>
         Look up WCAG. The data ships in the package, so these commands open no browser and
         make no network request.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>wcag</code></dt>
         <dd>In a terminal, an interactive finder: type to search, read the criterion beside the list.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag &lt;criterion&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>One criterion by number or slug: the requirement, how to test it, and what to do when it fails. Also takes a technique ID such as <code>G18</code>. <code>wcag show</code> is the same command.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag criteria</code></dt>
         <dd>List criteria. <code>--level</code> narrows the list. <code>--summary</code> counts them by <a href="/test-methods">test method</a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag understanding &lt;criterion&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The W3C's full Understanding document for the criterion.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag rule &lt;ruleId&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The criteria one axe rule tests, with axe's help text.</dd>
         <dt><code>search &lt;query&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Search criteria, techniques, axe rules, and ARIA patterns in one ranked list. <code>--kind</code> keeps one kind: <code>criterion</code>, <code>technique</code>, <code>failure</code>, <code>axe-rule</code>, <code>pattern</code>, or <code>example</code>. <code>--limit</code> defaults to 10.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 wcag 1.4.3
a1 wcag status-messages --json
a1 wcag criteria --level AA
a1 wcag rule color-contrast
a1 search "focus order"</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="pattern">a1 pattern</h2>
      <p>
         Looks up the W3C's
         <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/">ARIA Authoring Practices Guide</a>, which
         documents how widgets such as comboboxes and dialogs should behave, and checks a
         live widget against it.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>pattern</code></dt>
         <dd>List every pattern. <code>pattern list</code> does the same.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern &lt;name&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>One pattern, such as <code>combobox</code>, or one of its examples, such as <code>combobox-select-only</code>, with its keyboard and attribute tables. <code>--section</code> keeps <code>about</code>, <code>keyboard</code>, <code>attributes</code>, or <code>examples</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern role &lt;role&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The examples that use one ARIA role.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern attribute &lt;attribute&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The examples that use one attribute, such as <code>aria-expanded</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern check [target]</code></dt>
         <dd>Press every key an example documents on your widget, and check its attributes. Needs <code>--pattern &lt;exampleId&gt;</code> and <code>--selector &lt;css&gt;</code>. <code>--click</code> opens the widget first. <code>--table</code> and <code>--setup</code> reach a later state of it.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern record &lt;target&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Record your judgment of one row the check could not decide. Needs <code>--pattern</code>, <code>--row</code>, <code>--selector</code>, and <code>--outcome</code>: <code>passed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>cantTell</code>, or <code>inapplicable</code>. <code>--note</code> says why, <code>--by</code> says who decided, and <code>--mode</code> is <code>manual</code> or <code>semiAutomatic</code>. Pass the same <code>--click</code> the check used.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern pending &lt;target&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The rows with no judgment yet. A judgment made before the widget changed no longer counts.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 pattern combobox
a1 pattern combobox-select-only --section keyboard
a1 pattern check http://localhost:3000 --pattern dialog --selector '[role="dialog"]' --click '#open-settings'</code></pre>
      <p>
         <code>pattern check</code> exits 4 for two findings: a documented key that did
         nothing, and an attribute that is missing. It prints every other key beside the
         guide's description of what should happen, for you to judge. Judgments are kept in
         <code>.a11ied/evidence.jsonl</code>. <code>--results &lt;path&gt;</code> on
         <code>check</code>, <code>record</code>, and <code>pending</code> names another file.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="audit">a1 audit</h2>
      <p>
         Tracks a WCAG audit that your AI agents carry out, and writes the report. See
         <a href="/guides/audit">audit a site with AI agents</a>. Every subcommand except <code>init</code>
         and <code>list</code> takes <code>--audit &lt;id&gt;</code>. Without it, a1 uses
         <code>$A11IED_AUDIT</code>, then the only audit in the workspace.
      </p>
      <h3>Set up</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>audit init &lt;target&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Create an audit. <code>--name</code>, <code>--id</code>, <code>--platform web|ios|android</code>, <code>--level</code>, <code>--wcag</code>, <code>--criteria</code>, <code>--passes</code>, <code>--rule</code>, <code>--access</code>, and <code>--page</code> for one page only.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit list</code></dt>
         <dd>The audits in this workspace.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit page add &lt;locator&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Add a page, screen, state, or flow. <code>--name</code>, <code>--kind</code>, <code>--notes</code>, <code>--group</code>, <code>--passes</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit page list</code>, <code>exclude</code>, <code>include</code></dt>
         <dd>Review and change what the audit covers. <code>exclude</code> needs <code>--reason</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit discover [url]</code></dt>
         <dd>Find a site's pages and add them. <code>--max-pages</code>, default 50, <code>--include</code>, <code>--exclude</code>, <code>--storage-state</code>, <code>--dry-run</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit scan</code></dt>
         <dd>Run the automated checks on every web page. <code>--page</code>, <code>--concurrency</code>, default 4, <code>--timeout</code>, default 30000, <code>--storage-state</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Do the work</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>audit next --worker &lt;name&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Claim a unit and print its work packet. <code>--pass</code>, <code>--not-pass</code>, <code>--page</code>, <code>--unit</code>, <code>--lease &lt;minutes&gt;</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit show &lt;unit&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Print a unit's packet without claiming it.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit submit &lt;unit&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Submit results. Needs <code>--worker</code> and <code>--file &lt;json&gt;</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit note &lt;unit&gt; [message]</code></dt>
         <dd>Keep a claim alive and log progress.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit block &lt;unit&gt; --reason</code></dt>
         <dd>Set aside a unit that needs a person. <code>--worker</code> records who blocked it.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit reopen &lt;unit&gt; --reason</code></dt>
         <dd>Put a blocked or finished unit back in the queue.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit limitation [text]</code></dt>
         <dd>Record something the whole audit could not test. <code>--criterion</code>, <code>--list</code>, <code>--remove</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3>Watch and report</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>audit status</code></dt>
         <dd>Progress, workers, blocked units, and recent activity. <code>--units</code> lists every unit.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit log</code></dt>
         <dd>The activity log. <code>--unit</code>, and <code>--limit</code>, default 50.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit dashboard</code></dt>
         <dd>Serve a live progress page. <code>--port</code>, default 4173, or <code>--out &lt;file&gt;</code> for a snapshot.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit findings</code></dt>
         <dd>List findings. <code>--criterion</code>, <code>--page</code>, <code>--all</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit finding show|dismiss|merge|update</code></dt>
         <dd>Inspect or correct one finding.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit signals &lt;page&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>The measurements the scan took for a page. <code>--kind</code> keeps one kind.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit report</code></dt>
         <dd>Write the report as HTML, Markdown, and JSON. <code>--format</code>, <code>--out &lt;dir&gt;</code>, and <code>--link-evidence</code> to link screenshots in place of embedding them.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="doctor">a1 doctor</h2>
      <p>
         <code>a1 doctor</code> checks this machine and lists the setup steps still needed,
         each with its command.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>--task &lt;task&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Check for <code>scan</code>, <code>reader</code>, <code>audit</code>, or <code>all</code>, the default.</dd>
         <dt><code>--sr &lt;reader&gt;</code></dt>
         <dd>Check <code>voiceover</code>, <code>nvda</code>, or <code>virtual</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>--recording</code></dt>
         <dd>With <code>--task reader</code> or <code>audit</code>, also check screen recording. On macOS this records a short test video and deletes it.</dd>
         <dt><code>--strict</code></dt>
         <dd>Exit 3 when a required step is missing. Without it, <code>doctor</code> exits 0.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 doctor
a1 doctor --task reader --sr voiceover --recording
a1 doctor --strict</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="setup">a1 setup</h2>
      <p>
         Run it once on each machine. Before a global install, run it as
         <code>npx a11ied setup</code>. It asks before each step:
      </p>
      <ol>
         <li>If <code>a1</code> is not installed globally, it offers to install it with npm.</li>
         <li>
            It finds the AI coding agents on this machine, such as Claude Code, Codex, and
            Cursor, and offers to add the a11ied skills and the MCP server to them. The skills,
            the MCP server, and each agent are checkboxes. They are installed for every
            project. Running setup again updates them.
         </li>
         <li>
            It offers to run the Guidepup setup that VoiceOver and NVDA sessions need. This
            changes system settings. The simulated screen reader needs no setup.
         </li>
         <li>It runs <code>doctor</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>-y</code>, <code>--yes</code></dt>
         <dd>Do every step without asking, for every agent it finds.</dd>
         <dt><code>--json</code></dt>
         <dd>Print JSON. It never asks, so without <code>--yes</code> only the screen reader steps run.</dd>
         <dt><code>--skip-setup</code></dt>
         <dd>Skip the macOS permission step.</dd>
         <dt><code>--skip-install</code></dt>
         <dd>Skip the screen reader download.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         It exits 3 when a step failed or one is still missing. The agents are set up with
         <a href="https://aix.a1st.dev/">aix</a>. To remove them, run
         <code>npx -y @a1st/aix remove skill a11ied</code>,
         <code>npx -y @a1st/aix remove skill a11ied-audit</code>, and
         <code>npx -y @a1st/aix remove mcp a11ied</code>.
      </p>
      <pre><code>npx a11ied setup
a1 setup --yes --skip-setup</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="update">a1 update</h2>
      <p>
         Asks the npm registry for the latest version of a11ied. If it is newer, it asks,
         then runs <code>npm install --global a11ied@&lt;version&gt;</code>. When a11ied is a
         dependency of a project, it changes nothing and prints the command to run in that
         project.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>-y</code>, <code>--yes</code></dt>
         <dd>Install without asking.</dd>
         <dt><code>--json</code></dt>
         <dd>Print JSON. It never asks, so it installs only with <code>--yes</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre><code>a1 update
a1 update --yes</code></pre>
      <h3 id="update-notice">Update notices</h3>
      <p>
         Once a day, a1 checks for a newer version in a background process. When it finds
         one, <code>a1</code>, <code>a1 --help</code>, and <code>a1 doctor</code> print a short
         notice at the end of their output. The notice is never printed with
         <code>--json</code> or <code>--version</code>, when the output is not a terminal, or
         in CI. The <a href="#audit">audit dashboard</a> shows the same notice as a banner you
         can dismiss.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="other">a1 mcp and a1 help-all</h2>
      <p>
         <code>a1 mcp</code> starts the <a href="/reference/mcp">MCP server</a> on standard
         input and output. It takes no options.
      </p>
      <p>
         <code>a1 help-all</code> prints the help for every command in one response. Give it
         to an agent that works through the terminal.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="exit-codes">Exit codes</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>0</dt>
         <dd>The command ran and nothing it checked failed.</dd>
         <dt>1</dt>
         <dd>An unknown command or option, or a missing argument.</dd>
         <dt>2</dt>
         <dd>Usage error: an option value that is not allowed, or no active session.</dd>
         <dt>3</dt>
         <dd>The machine is not ready.</dd>
         <dt>4</dt>
         <dd>A check failed.</dd>
         <dt>5</dt>
         <dd>An unclassified error.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>See <a href="/guides/scripting#exit-codes">script the CLI</a>.</p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="environment">Environment</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>A11IED_STATE_DIR</code></dt>
         <dd>Where the active session's state is kept. Default: <code>$XDG_STATE_HOME/a11ied</code>, then <code>~/.a11ied/state</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>A11IED_AUDIT</code></dt>
         <dd>The audit that <code>a1 audit</code> commands use when <code>--audit</code> is not given.</dd>
         <dt><code>A11IED_AUDITS_DIR</code></dt>
         <dd>Where audits are kept. Default: <code>.a11ied/audits</code> in the working directory.</dd>
         <dt><code>A11IED_EVIDENCE</code></dt>
         <dd>The file of <code>pattern record</code> judgments. Default: <code>.a11ied/evidence.jsonl</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER</code></dt>
         <dd>Set to any value to turn off the daily update check and its notices.</dd>
         <dt><code>A11IED_DRIVER_MODE</code></dt>
         <dd><code>in-process</code> keeps a simulated session inside the calling process. By default a session runs in a separate process, so it outlives the command that started it.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         a1 uses an installed Chrome, Edge, Brave, or Chromium before Playwright's own
         Chromium. <code>a1 doctor</code> shows which one it found.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
